  "faqs": [
    [
      "What should a small business website maintenance checklist include?",
      "Include uptime monitoring, backup verification, software and security updates, form and checkout testing, broken-link checks, mobile performance, content reviews, search indexing, account access and renewal dates. Give every task an owner and a completion check."
    ],
    [
      "How often should a small business website be maintained?",
      "Monitor critical availability and backup alerts daily or automatically, test customer journeys weekly, review content and SEO monthly, test recovery quarterly and review renewals annually. Increase the frequency for busy stores and handle urgent security problems immediately."
    ],
    [
      "Can I maintain my business website myself?",
      "You can review business information, test forms and links, and keep a maintenance log. Assign software changes, recovery and complex errors to someone who can test, diagnose and roll back changes safely."
    ],
    [
      "Does website hosting include maintenance?",
      "Some plans include selected updates, backups or monitoring, but hosting alone does not establish that forms, content, integrations or recovery are being checked. Confirm each responsibility in the service scope."
    ],
    [
      "How much does website maintenance cost?",
      "Cost depends on the platform, integrations, change volume and response requirements. Compare itemized quotes for routine checks, software licences, backups, content hours and emergency support rather than relying on one average price."
    ],
    [
      "Will website maintenance improve Google rankings?",
      "Maintenance can address crawling problems, broken pages and poor user experience. Rankings also depend on content relevance and other signals. Neither routine updates nor an indexing request guarantees first-page rankings."
    ]
  ],
